                  "width": "fill_container(322)",
                  "content": "Tubable means the dam's total release (น้ำออกเขื่อน) is at least 0.8 million m³ a day. The irrigation canals take the first ~0.37; the rest flows down the Mae Ngat.",
                  "fontFamily": "$font-body",
                  "fontSize": 14,
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "SOVUN",
                  "x": 18,
                  "y": 158,
                  "name": "P",
                  "enabled": false,
                  "fill": "$ink",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container(322)",
                  "content": "The forecast is a model trained on every day since 2006. It starts from how full the dam is and how much it is releasing now (95% full, 0.42 M m³/day on 9 Oct). Current release drives the next few weeks; fullness drives the months after. Window odds show the stretch average. Rainfall and El Niño were tested and didn't improve it, so they're shown for context only.",
                  "fontFamily": "$font-body",
                  "fontSize": 14,
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "OLtKK",
                  "x": 18,
                  "y": 314,
                  "name": "P",
                  "enabled": false,
                  "fill": "$ink",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container(322)",
                  "content": "Data: Royal Irrigation Department daily reservoir reports, Open-Meteo catchment rainfall, NOAA Oceanic Niño Index.",
                  "fontFamily": "$font-body",
                  "fontSize": 14,
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                }
              ]
            },
